**Homelessness — BLANK `direction-only`**

The single snapshot gives one usable passage: the Indiana Capital Chronicle's direct quotation of Randolph during debate (`own-words`, `on-question`, `statement-other`, 2026-02-27, `in-term`).

Why no chair:
- He rejects jail ("not jail time") and names services instead. That excludes rung 5's criminal penalties and leans away from enforcement generally, but it does not separate rung 1 (no penalties of any kind), rung 2 (decriminalizing), or rung 3 (enforcement only when shelter beds are available). He says nothing about civil penalties, so rung 4 isn't excluded either.
- This is V4.2: ruling out the criminal-penalty rung is not evidence for whichever rung is left.
